ameisnt.kim\/sunwatch\/gallery\/uploads\/1728167132953.jpg"},{"id":1729461360144,"city":"Kittery Point, Maine","cover":14,"ceiling":34082,"temperature":65,"visibility":11,"comments":"I'm rewriting this whole website. the vision for it all came to me in a dream last night (seriously) and it's gonna be fking badass... I'll likely keep this version public as v2.sunwat.ch but we'll see \ud83d\ude09","imageUrl":"https:\/\/mynameisnt.kim\/sunwatch\/gallery\/uploads\/1729461360144.jpg"},{"id":1731631542094,"city":"South Berwick, Maine","cover":11,"ceiling":30000,"temperature":22,"visibility":10,"comments":"not a sunset, but an advertisement lol. I said I was rewriting this app, and boy have I been. Using an open source weather API now, looking in the actual direction of the sunrise or sunset for weather data. A rating algorithm that's 300 lines long. 126kb of raw data parsed into an elegant, responsive, and dynamic UI. I'm super happy with this version of Sunwatch. It's still in active development, but you can get an early access preview at https:\/\/swv3.com\/ \nSome things are broken, but the main functionality is here and working :)","imageUrl":"https:\/\/mynameisnt.kim\/sunwatch\/gallery\/uploads\/1731631542094.png"}]